 ### Aokana
-Streaming/LOD variant of DAG that splits the world into many shallow DAGs of 256³ Voxels each, with octree-style LOD levels (LOD n is 8 children merged at the same 256³ resolution) and distance-based streaming [S2]. On an RTX 3060 Ti it renders a 64K scene of about 10 billion Voxels in about 6 ms. Only about 2–17% of the data is resident: 424 MB VRAM against 23 GB on disk for San Miguel at 64K [S2]. In Aokana's numbers, colour dominates storage: 21 GB of colour against 2.2 GB of geometry [S2]. Game attributes cannot utilize complex lossy compression [S2].
+Aokana is a streaming/LOD variant of DAG that splits the world into many shallow DAGs of 256³ Voxels each, with octree-style LOD levels (LOD n is 8 children merged at the same 256³ resolution) and distance-based streaming [S2]. On an RTX 3060 Ti it renders a 64K scene of about 10 billion Voxels in about 6 ms [S2]. Only about 2–17% of the data is resident: 424 MB VRAM against 23 GB on disk for San Miguel at 64K [S2]. In Aokana's numbers, colour dominates storage: 21 GB of colour against 2.2 GB of geometry [S2]. Game attributes cannot utilize complex lossy compression [S2].
 
